# Skill install groups. Two record types, whitespace separated:
#   group <id> <description>   declares a group; the description is what an
#                              installer, a plugin manifest, or a picker shows
#   <skill> <group>            puts a skill in a declared group
# A skill with no record belongs to `core`, which always installs, and may name
# only one group. Keep LF line endings: the bash reader rejects CRLF loudly,
# the TypeScript reader trims and tolerates it — they only agree on LF.
# Adding a group is a `group` line plus its membership lines — nothing else.

group core Enforcement, review, planning, and workflow skills for everyday use
group product Product-model skills: evidence-backed briefs and product review

product-intelligence product
product-review product
